.Nd functions to assist in the creation of OSSL_PARAM arrays
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/param_build.h
.Ft typedef struct OSSL_PARAM_BLD;

 OSSL_PARAM_BLD *
.Fo OSSL_PARAM_BLD_new
.Fa void
.Fc
.Ft OSSL_PARAM *
.Fo OSSL_PARAM_BLD_to_param
.Fa "OSSL_PARAM_BLD *bld"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo OSSL_PARAM_BLD_free
.Fa "OSSL_PARAM_BLD *bld"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OSSL_PARAM_BLD_push_TYPE
.Fa "OSSL_PARAM_BLD *bld"
.Fa "const char *key"
.Fa "TYPE val"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OSSL_PARAM_BLD_push_BN
.Fa "OSSL_PARAM_BLD *bld"
.Fa "const char *key"
.Fa "const BIGNUM *bn"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OSSL_PARAM_BLD_push_BN_pad
.Fa "OSSL_PARAM_BLD *bld"
.Fa "const char *key"
.Fa "const BIGNUM *bn"
.Fa "size_t sz"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OSSL_PARAM_BLD_push_utf8_string
.Fa "OSSL_PARAM_BLD *bld"
.Fa "const char *key"
.Fa "const char *buf"
.Fa "size_t bsize"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OSSL_PARAM_BLD_push_utf8_ptr
.Fa "OSSL_PARAM_BLD *bld"
.Fa "const char *key"
.Fa "char *buf"
.Fa "size_t bsize"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OSSL_PARAM_BLD_push_octet_string
.Fa "OSSL_PARAM_BLD *bld"
.Fa "const char *key"
.Fa "const void *buf"
.Fa "size_t bsize"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OSSL_PARAM_BLD_push_octet_ptr
.Fa "OSSL_PARAM_BLD *bld"
.Fa "const char *key"
.Fa "void *buf"
.Fa "size_t bsize"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A collection of utility functions that simplify the creation of
OSSL_PARAM arrays.
The
.Sy Vt TYPE
names are as per
.Xr OSSL_PARAM_int 3 .
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_PARAM_BLD_new
allocates and initialises a new OSSL_PARAM_BLD structure so that values
can be added.
Any existing values are cleared.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_PARAM_BLD_free
deallocates the memory allocates by
.Fn OSSL_PARAM_BLD_new .
If the argument is NULL, nothing is done.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_PARAM_BLD_to_param
converts a built up OSSL_PARAM_BLD structure
.Fa bld
into an allocated OSSL_PARAM array.
The OSSL_PARAM array and all associated storage must be freed by calling
.Xr OSSL_PARAM_free 3
with the functions return value.
.Fn OSSL_PARAM_BLD_free
can safely be called any time after this function is.
.Pp
.Sy OSSL_PARAM_BLD_push_ Ns Vt TYPE Ns
.Xr 3
are a series of functions which will create OSSL_PARAM objects of the
specified size and correct type for the
.Fa val
argument.
.Fa val
is stored by value and an expression or auto variable can be used.
.Pp
When
.Sy Vt TYPE
denotes an integer type, signed integer types will normally get the
OSSL_PARAM type
.Sy OSSL_PARAM_INTEGER
params.
When
.Sy Vt TYPE
denotes an unsigned integer type will get the OSSL_PARAM type
.Sy OSSL_PARAM_UNSIGNED_INTEGER .
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_PARAM_BLD_push_BN
is a function that will create an OSSL_PARAM object that holds the
specified BIGNUM
.Fa bn .
When the
.Fa bn
is zero or positive, its OSSL_PARAM type becomes
.Sy OSSL_PARAM_UNSIGNED_INTEGER .
When the
.Fa bn
is negative, its OSSL_PARAM type becomes
.Sy OSSL_PARAM_INTEGER .
If
.Fa bn
is marked as being securely allocated, its OSSL_PARAM representation
will also be securely allocated.
The
.Fa bn
argument is stored by reference and the underlying BIGNUM object must
exist until after
.Fn OSSL_PARAM_BLD_to_param
has been called.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_PARAM_BLD_push_BN_pad
is a function that will create an OSSL_PARAM object that holds the
specified BIGNUM
.Fa bn .
The object will be padded to occupy exactly
.Fa sz
bytes, if insufficient space is specified an error results.
When the
.Fa bn
is zero or positive, its OSSL_PARAM type becomes
.Sy OSSL_PARAM_UNSIGNED_INTEGER .
When the
.Fa bn
is negative, its OSSL_PARAM type becomes
.Sy OSSL_PARAM_INTEGER .
If
.Fa bn
is marked as being securely allocated, its OSSL_PARAM representation
will also be securely allocated.
The
.Fa bn
argument is stored by reference and the underlying BIGNUM object must
exist until after
.Fn OSSL_PARAM_BLD_to_param
has been called.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_PARAM_BLD_push_utf8_string
is a function that will create an OSSL_PARAM object that references the
UTF8 string specified by
.Fa buf .
The length of the string
.Fa bsize
should not include the terminating NUL byte.
If it is zero then it will be calculated.
The string that
.Fa buf
points to is stored by reference and must remain in scope until after
.Fn OSSL_PARAM_BLD_to_param
has been called.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_PARAM_BLD_push_octet_string
is a function that will create an OSSL_PARAM object that references the
octet string specified by
.Fa buf
and <bsize>. The memory that
.Fa buf
points to is stored by reference and must remain in scope until after
.Fn OSSL_PARAM_BLD_to_param
has been called.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_PARAM_BLD_push_utf8_ptr
is a function that will create an OSSL_PARAM object that references the
UTF8 string specified by
.Fa buf .
The length of the string
.Fa bsize
should not include the terminating NUL byte.
If it is zero then it will be calculated.
The string
.Fa buf
points to is stored by reference and must remain in scope until the
OSSL_PARAM array is freed.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_PARAM_BLD_push_octet_ptr
is a function that will create an OSSL_PARAM object that references the
octet string specified by
.Fa buf .
The memory
.Fa buf
points to is stored by reference and must remain in scope until the
OSSL_PARAM array is freed.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn OSSL_PARAM_BLD_new
returns the allocated OSSL_PARAM_BLD structure, or NULL on error.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_PARAM_BLD_to_param
returns the allocated OSSL_PARAM array, or NULL on error.
.Pp
All of the OSSL_PARAM_BLD_push_TYPE functions return 1 on success and 0
on error.
.Sh NOTES
.Fn OSSL_PARAM_BLD_push_BN
and
.Fn OSSL_PARAM_BLD_push_BN_pad
only support nonnegative
.Sy BIGNUM Ns s.
They return an error on negative
.Sy BIGNUM Ns s.
To pass signed
.Sy BIGNUM Ns s,
use
.Xr OSSL_PARAM_BLD_push_signed_BN 3 .
.Sh EXAMPLES
Both examples creating an OSSL_PARAM array that contains an RSA key.
For both, the predefined key variables are:
.Bd -literal
    BIGNUM *n;           /* modulus */
    unsigned int e;      /* public exponent */
    BIGNUM *d;           /* private exponent */
    BIGNUM *p, *q;       /* first two prime factors */
    BIGNUM *dmp1, *dmq1; /* first two CRT exponents */
    BIGNUM *iqmp;        /* first CRT coefficient */
.Ed
.Ss Example 1
This example shows how to create an OSSL_PARAM array that contains an
RSA private key.
.Bd -literal
    OSSL_PARAM_BLD *bld = OSSL_PARAM_BLD_new();
    OSSL_PARAM *params = NULL;

    if (bld == NULL
        || !OSSL_PARAM_BLD_push_BN(bld, "n", n)
        || !OSSL_PARAM_BLD_push_uint(bld, "e", e)
        || !OSSL_PARAM_BLD_push_BN(bld, "d", d)
        || !OSSL_PARAM_BLD_push_BN(bld, "rsa-factor1", p)
        || !OSSL_PARAM_BLD_push_BN(bld, "rsa-factor2", q)
        || !OSSL_PARAM_BLD_push_BN(bld, "rsa-exponent1", dmp1)
        || !OSSL_PARAM_BLD_push_BN(bld, "rsa-exponent2", dmq1)
        || !OSSL_PARAM_BLD_push_BN(bld, "rsa-coefficient1", iqmp)
        || (params = OSSL_PARAM_BLD_to_param(bld)) == NULL)
        goto err;
    OSSL_PARAM_BLD_free(bld);
    /* Use params */
    ...
    OSSL_PARAM_free(params);
.Ed
.Ss Example 2
This example shows how to create an OSSL_PARAM array that contains an
RSA public key.
.Bd -literal
    OSSL_PARAM_BLD *bld = OSSL_PARAM_BLD_new();
    OSSL_PARAM *params = NULL;

    if (nld == NULL
        || !OSSL_PARAM_BLD_push_BN(bld, "n", n)
        || !OSSL_PARAM_BLD_push_uint(bld, "e", e)
        || (params = OSSL_PARAM_BLD_to_param(bld)) == NULL)
        goto err;
    OSSL_PARAM_BLD_free(bld);
    /* Use params */
    ...
    OSSL_PARAM_free(params);
.Ed
